      en: ["Sant'Agata is named after the co-patron saint of San Marino.", "The site commemorates the liberation from Alberoni occupation on Feb 5, 1740.", "The region features significant religious structures built from local sandstone.", "A major annual procession is held here on Saint Agatha's feast day.", "The area is strategically located at the foot of Mount Titano.", "It is included within the UNESCO World Heritage area of the old town."],
